00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.305
and Timothy Dwight Colleges.

00:20:35.305 --> 00:20:38.055
(crowd cheering)

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:42.010
And welcome to family, friends

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:45.210
and members of the class who
are joining us virtually today

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.333
via live stream.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:50.900
We are so excited to have
arrived at this special day.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:54.170
In a few moments, we will
begin announcing the graduates

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:57.973
as they process across this
stage here in front of me.

00:20:58.850 --> 00:21:00.800
But before we start our program,

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:02.630
a few words about the land

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:05.840
on which today's ceremony is taking place.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:09.060
Yale acknowledges that
indigenous peoples and nations

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:14.060
including Mohegan, Mashantucket
Pequot, Eastern Pequot,

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:19.003
Schaghticoke, Golden
Hill Paugussett, Niantic,

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:24.170
and the Quinnipiac and other
Algonquian speaking peoples

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:27.620
have stewarded through generations
the lands and waterways

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:30.320
of what is now the State of Connecticut.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:33.920
We honor and respect the
enduring relationship that exists

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:37.550
between these peoples and
nations and this land.

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:39.500
Thank you and please enjoy the program.

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:46.210
