01:02:11.490 --> 01:02:14.820
- To the students of the class of 2021

01:02:15.880 --> 01:02:19.470
and their parents, families
and friends looking on

01:02:19.470 --> 01:02:21.583
from around the globe.

01:02:23.080 --> 01:02:27.040
We gather to recognize the
extraordinary accomplishments

01:02:27.040 --> 01:02:30.230
of all of you who have worked so hard

01:02:30.230 --> 01:02:32.283
to complete your programs of study.

01:02:33.410 --> 01:02:37.700
We salute your effort,
your diligence, your talent

01:02:37.700 --> 01:02:38.763
and your intellect.

01:02:39.850 --> 01:02:44.100
We also join you in expressing gratitude

01:02:44.100 --> 01:02:47.660
for all who have supported
you in these endeavors,

01:02:47.660 --> 01:02:52.170
your families and friends and teachers

01:02:52.170 --> 01:02:54.293
and other members of the Yale community.

01:02:55.700 --> 01:03:00.302
Congratulations, class of 2021.

01:03:00.302 --> 01:03:05.302
(crowd cheering)
(crowd clapping)

01:03:16.193 --> 01:03:18.060
- Hello, class of 2021.

01:03:18.060 --> 01:03:21.228
My name is Curtis Colvett
and I'm your class treasurer.

01:03:21.228 --> 01:03:22.750
(crowd cheering)
(crowd clapping)

01:03:22.750 --> 01:03:25.270
Four years have gone by
in the blink of an eye.

01:03:25.270 --> 01:03:26.990
We've made so many memories

01:03:26.990 --> 01:03:29.690
from the first year
snowball fight on old campus

01:03:29.690 --> 01:03:32.700
to the Yale Harvard football
game in 2019, where we've won

01:03:32.700 --> 01:03:34.210
in double overtime.

01:03:34.210 --> 01:03:35.740
To all of the late nights,

01:03:35.740 --> 01:03:38.260
whether they be in the
library studying for an exam

01:03:38.260 --> 01:03:40.690
or in the common room,
talking with our friends

01:03:40.690 --> 01:03:41.663
and suite-mates.

01:03:42.580 --> 01:03:44.230
Although our senior year,

01:03:44.230 --> 01:03:46.230
experience was certainly
not a traditional one,

01:03:46.230 --> 01:03:50.240
the class of 2021 made
the best of the situation.

01:03:50.240 --> 01:03:53.060
When we leave Yale in just a few days,

01:03:53.060 --> 01:03:54.380
we will leave with memories

01:03:54.380 --> 01:03:57.800
and friendships that will last a lifetime.

01:03:57.800 --> 01:03:59.410
Here's to the class of 2021.

01:03:59.410 --> 01:04:01.218
We did it, congratulations.

01:04:01.218 --> 01:04:06.218
(crowd cheering)
(crowd clapping)

01:04:20.390 --> 01:04:23.877
- Class of 2021, good afternoon.

01:04:23.877 --> 01:04:28.877
(crowd cheering)
(crowd clapping)

01:04:29.360 --> 01:04:30.980
My name is Akhil Rajan,

01:04:30.980 --> 01:04:33.750
and I'm a member of the committee
that organized Class Day

01:04:33.750 --> 01:04:37.830
which will air on YouTube
tomorrow at 2:30 PM.

01:04:37.830 --> 01:04:40.160
Two minutes before at 2:28,

01:04:40.160 --> 01:04:43.880
a special piece written by
Class Day speaker, Robert Lopez

01:04:43.880 --> 01:04:46.020
will be played from Harkness Tower

01:04:46.020 --> 01:04:47.930
so keep your ears open.

01:04:47.930 --> 01:04:50.150
And if you haven't already
decorated a funny hat

01:04:50.150 --> 01:04:52.760
for Class Day, it's not too late.

01:04:52.760 --> 01:04:54.600
In fact, on your seat today,

01:04:54.600 --> 01:04:57.350
you received a Class of 2021 hat

01:04:57.350 --> 01:05:00.160
which you might wanna use
for that very purpose.

01:05:00.160 --> 01:05:02.420
You'll also find a gift
bag, which includes items

01:05:02.420 --> 01:05:05.670
that represent longstanding
Class Day traditions

01:05:05.670 --> 01:05:09.930
as well as a few that are
unique to the Class of 2021.

01:05:09.930 --> 01:05:11.810
In addition to the Class Day speaker,

01:05:11.810 --> 01:05:14.050
tomorrow's program will
also include remarks

01:05:14.050 --> 01:05:15.720
by members of our class

01:05:15.720 --> 01:05:18.751
who've put together outstanding speeches

01:05:18.751 --> 01:05:22.840
and because Class Day is about all of us,

01:05:22.840 --> 01:05:24.070
you'll see your photographs

01:05:24.070 --> 01:05:27.500
and video reflections throughout
tomorrow's program as well.

01:05:27.500 --> 01:05:29.800
Congratulations, class of 2021

01:05:29.800 --> 01:05:31.885
and see you tomorrow at class.

01:05:31.885 --> 01:05:36.885
(crowd cheering)
(crowd clapping)

01:05:47.670 --> 01:05:50.650
- Class of 2021, congratulations again,

01:05:50.650 --> 01:05:54.510
I am so happy to be with you
and celebrate with you today.

01:05:54.510 --> 01:05:57.200
Graduating is such a great accomplishment

01:05:57.200 --> 01:05:59.990
and one of the most
important ones in your life.

01:05:59.990 --> 01:06:03.320
If you think back to when
you first arrived on campus,

01:06:03.320 --> 01:06:04.370
no one could have imagined

01:06:04.370 --> 01:06:06.880
that you would live
through a global pandemic

01:06:06.880 --> 01:06:09.990
before reaching this moment, but you did.

01:06:09.990 --> 01:06:12.130
And thanks to your
strength and perseverance

01:06:12.130 --> 01:06:14.600
this moment has finally come.

01:06:14.600 --> 01:06:18.660
I am honored to recognize all
the work that you have done

01:06:18.660 --> 01:06:20.860
to get here, much of it with the support

01:06:20.860 --> 01:06:22.710
of your family and friends.

01:06:22.710 --> 01:06:24.110
Today is your day,

01:06:24.110 --> 01:06:25.403
and it is there's too.

01:06:26.710 --> 01:06:28.990
Today's the day for
looking back with pride

01:06:28.990 --> 01:06:30.760
at everything you have accomplished

01:06:30.760 --> 01:06:32.860
and all the goals you have reached.

01:06:32.860 --> 01:06:35.200
Of course, it brings some sadness too

01:06:35.200 --> 01:06:38.520
now that you are ending
your bright college years.

01:06:38.520 --> 01:06:40.800
But today is a commencement, a beginning.

01:06:40.800 --> 01:06:43.850
So now as you look to
the days and years ahead,

01:06:43.850 --> 01:06:46.340
think of the new achievements
and opportunities

01:06:46.340 --> 01:06:47.680
in front of you,

01:06:47.680 --> 01:06:50.680
and look around as well to remind yourself

01:06:50.680 --> 01:06:54.170
of the excellent company joining
you on this new beginning,

01:06:54.170 --> 01:06:56.894
your friendships formed at Yale.

01:06:56.894 --> 01:06:59.360
Tomorrow you will celebrate Class Day,

01:06:59.360 --> 01:07:02.130
a tradition stretching back 150 years

01:07:02.130 --> 01:07:04.100
in Yale College history.

01:07:04.100 --> 01:07:07.730
I'm excited to watch the
virtual program alongside you,

01:07:07.730 --> 01:07:09.360
and on Monday we can look forward

01:07:09.360 --> 01:07:12.580
to President Salovey's
commencement address.

01:07:12.580 --> 01:07:14.800
I am grateful to the Class Day committee,

01:07:14.800 --> 01:07:16.720
to the senior class council,

01:07:16.720 --> 01:07:19.710
to the university Secretary's Office,

01:07:19.710 --> 01:07:21.470
to your college heads and deans

01:07:21.470 --> 01:07:24.701
and to everyone who contributed
to making the special events

01:07:24.701 --> 01:07:27.121
of this weekend possible.

01:07:27.121 --> 01:07:30.030
And I'm most appreciative to you

01:07:30.030 --> 01:07:32.210
for all that you have brought to Yale,

01:07:32.210 --> 01:07:35.460
and now we'll bring out
into the world with you.

01:07:35.460 --> 01:07:38.015
Again, Class of 2021, congratulations.

01:07:38.015 --> 01:07:43.015
(crowd cheering)
(crowd clapping)

01:07:47.570 --> 01:07:50.153
(bright music)

01:15:02.447 --> 01:15:05.030
(upbeat music)

